{
  "comment": "Descriptor floor conformance fixture (Common Agent 4.9, with 6.2's minimal Descriptor, 6.6's signature and 4.4's exchange 2). Every agent serves a bound, signed Descriptor that holds at least the minimal Descriptor's members. Pins which served Descriptors meet the floor, with signatures that really verify, and which answers to the entryway's descriptor exchange conform. Keys are spelled as Agent Messaging spells them, and the one seed is the published test seed its fixtures already use, so no new private-key-shaped string enters the repository; the second identity's seed is unpublished, which is why only the first identity signs. Signatures are Section 8.1's: Ed25519, base64, over the ASCII tag, one newline, and the JCS canonical JSON of the document without signatures. Check it with node conformance/lib/check-descriptor-floor.mjs. THE FIXTURE IS THE AUTHORITY: when a test against it fails, fix the implementation; change the fixture only with a spec change alongside.",
